Architecture note: this P7 page is self-contained (one `@Observable IngestXRayPageModel` exposing typed state +
load()/refresh()/reloadReport(), per the prompt's screen-scaffold spec) and matches the established sibling-page
convention (Sources/Features/Admin/{ApiPlayground,DiskForecast,FleetTelemetryCoverage}Page). It REUSES the pure P3
X-Ray adapters from the component library so the values are byte-identical to the standalone components (covenant #7,
"depends on component library (P3)"): XRayHeaderProjection / XRayStat / IngestXRayWindow / IngestXRaySummary
(XRayHeader.Adapter), IngestXRayBucket / XRayVehicleRef / XRayControlOption / XRayControlsProjection
(XRayControls.Adapter), XRayFieldStat / XRayFieldsSortKey / XRaySortDirection / XRayFieldsModel.nextSort
(XRayFieldsTable.Model), XRayFieldsProjector / XRayFieldRow / XRayValueKind / XRayNumberFormat / XRayRelativeTime /
XRayFieldsAccessibility (XRayFieldsTable.Adapter), XRayBucketInput / XRayBucketBar / XRayBucketChartProjection
(XRayBucketChart.{Models,Adapter}). It renders through the real P2 tokens + P3 base components (TSGlassPanel /
TSCard / TSChartContainer / TSBarChart / TSEmptyState / TSSpinner / TSButton / TSPageTitle / TSPanelTitle / TSCaption).

Navigation note: the sibling DiskForecast page already hosts on .admin; the first-segment parser would route /admin/*
there. To keep this page reachable + deep-linkable WITHOUT displacing the predecessor (covenant #7), a dedicated
.ingestXRay route (System sidebar group) plus an explicit /admin/ingest-xray alias were added — mirroring exactly how
the FleetTelemetryCoverage predecessor added .fleetTelemetryCoverage + /admin/telemetry/coverage. AppRoute.allCases
drives the sidebar / tabs / menu commands, so the new case is covered automatically; the new pathSegment is unique.

